<PARA INFOID = "T120021K387" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "16May2006"     INFOTYPE = "SYSTEM" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Hands-free Calling Function</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>G-BOOK ALPHA, a further evolution of the G-BOOK function, has been adopted to provide excellent functionality.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>By using the voice recognition microphone, telephone switch and a Bluetooth-compatible cellular phone, convenient functions such as "Hands-free Calling", "HELPNET" and "G-BOOK ALPHA" can be used.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>

<MECA ID = "T120021K387Ka75" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "10Jun2005"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Hands-free Calling</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>Wireless hands-free calling is possible using a Bluetooth-compatible cellular phone.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740061e" WIDTH = "6.903in" HEIGHT = "4.736in" />
</FIGURE>
<HINT>
<PTXT>Only specified models of cellular phone can be used.</PTXT></HINT>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>After a call is made or received, the conversation takes place through the voice recognition microphone and a vehicle speaker (front speaker RH).</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<LIST1><TITLE>Voice Recognition Microphone</TITLE>
<ITEM><PTXT>The voice recognition microphone is a unidirectional box-type microphone and is installed at the rear of the front personal lamp.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<LIST1><TITLE>Talk Switch/Telephone Switch</TITLE>
<ITEM><PTXT>The talk switch and telephone switch are located on the right side of the steering pad, allowing switch operation without taking the hands off the steering wheel.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T120021K387K448" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "14Apr2004"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Outgoing Calls</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>When the vehicle is stopped, pressing the off-hook switch of the telephone switch, or touching "TEL" on the information mode screen displayed by pressing the "Information/G" panel switch, changes the screen to the telephone number input screen, from which calls can be made by the following methods.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<INDICATE ID = "T120021K387K448I01" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Telephone Screen</TITLE>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "k4670093e" WIDTH = "2.847in" HEIGHT = "1.639in" />
</FIGURE>
</INDICATE>
<INDICATE ID = "T120021K387K448I02" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Dialing Methods</TITLE>
<TABLE FRAME = "ALL" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1">
<TGROUP COLS = "2" COLSEP = "1" ROWSEP = "1" TGROUPSTYLE = "Table_10">
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "1" COLNAME = "1" COLWIDTH = "25%"/>
<COLSPEC COLNUM = "2" COLNAME = "2" COLWIDTH = "74%"/>
<THEAD>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Item</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Method</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</THEAD>
<TBODY VALIGN = "MIDDLE">
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" ALIGN = "CENTER" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Dial Call</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Enter a telephone number to make a call.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" ALIGN = "CENTER" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Phonebook Call</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Call up a telephone number from the phonebook to make a call.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "1">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" ALIGN = "CENTER" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>One-touch Dial Call</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Select a pre-registered telephone number (one-touch dial) to make a call.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
<ROW ROWSEP = "0">
<ENTRY COLNAME = "1" ALIGN = "CENTER" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>History Call</PTXT></ENTRY>
<ENTRY COLNAME = "2" CONSPIC = "0"><PTXT>Call up a number previously called or a number from which a call was previously received to make a call.</PTXT></ENTRY>
</ROW>
</TBODY>
</TGROUP>
<LEGEND><HINT>
<PTXT>In addition to the above basic calling functions, calls can be made from the navigation screen (when telephone number data is available) and by voice recognition, allowing calls to be made in various situations.</PTXT></HINT></LEGEND></TABLE></INDICATE></MECA>

<MECA ID = "T120021K387K449" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "14Apr2004"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Incoming Calls</TITLE>
<LIST1><ITEM><PTXT>When a call is received, a ringtone sounds<HINTREF REFID = "H403120021K387K44901"/> and the incoming call screen is displayed. When the ringtone is output, the audio sound and navigation voice guidance are muted.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<HINT>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT ID = "H403120021K387K44901">With some cellular phones, the ringtone does not sound.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></HINT>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A call can be answered by touching "Talk (telephone mark)" on the incoming call screen or by pressing the off-hook switch of the telephone switch.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1></MECA>

